01:03:00,000 --> 01:03:06,000
Easy Riders, Raging Bulls: How the Sex-Drugs-and-Rock 'N Roll Generation Saved Hollywood is a book by Peter Biskind, published by Simon & Schuster in 1998, about ostensibly 1960s and 1970s Hollywood, a period of
American film known for the production of such films such as The Godfather, The Godfather Part II, The French Connection, Chinatown, Taxi Driver, Jaws, Star Wars, The Exorcist, and The Last Picture Show.

10
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
The book presents a comprehensive look into the people who influenced these
pictures and who continue to influence modern day filmmaking.

11
01:17:00,000 --> 01:17:06,000
The title is taken from films which bookend the era:
Easy Rider (1969) and Raging Bull (1980).

12
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
The book was the basis of a 2003 documentary film of the same title,
directed by Kenneth Bowser and narrated by actor William H.

13
01:31:00,000 --> 01:31:06,000
The documentary was screened out of competition
at the 2003 Cannes Film Festival.

14
